{#
    The Settings page's tabs, as links.

    Each tab is a page of its own — `/settings`, `/settings/data`,
    `/settings/instance` — so each works without script, can be bookmarked,
    and is answered by its own route: the Instance tab's 403 is the server's,
    not a hidden panel's. The rail lights Settings on all three.

    `aria-current="page"` marks the one being shown; the underline is drawn
    from it, so what the eye sees and what a screen reader is told are one
    fact. The Instance tab is offered only to an instance administrator,
    which is also who its route admits.
#}
<nav class="page-tabs" aria-label="{{ t('settings.tabs_label') }}">
    <ul class="page-tabs-list">
        <li>
            <a href="/settings" {{ tab == 'general' ? 'aria-current="page"' : '' }}>{{ t('settings.tab_general') }}</a>
        </li>
        <li>
            <a href="/settings/data" {{ tab == 'data' ? 'aria-current="page"' : '' }}>{{ t('settings.tab_data') }}</a>
        </li>
        {% if can(scope, 'instance.manage') %}
            <li>
                <a href="/settings/instance" {{ tab == 'instance' ? 'aria-current="page"' : '' }}>{{ t('settings.tab_instance') }}</a>
            </li>
        {% endif %}
    </ul>
</nav>
